One-line Summary: Add a column-level linear tile drain that leaves as a separate flux, routed to MOSART as surface runoff, with its nitrate going to nitrate runoff

Purpose of this version:
------------------------

Add tile drainage to CLM as a column flux, qflx_tile (mm H2O/s). Water is removed from the soil
column in the subsurface drainage routines, and then leaves the land as SURFACE runoff:

  - qflx_tile is a separate flux. It is NOT part of qflx_drain (still qflx_rsub_sat + rsub_top)
    and NOT added to qflx_surf_col.
  - total runoff: qflx_runoff = qflx_drain + qflx_surf + qflx_h2osfc_surf + qflx_qrgwl
                                + qflx_drain_perched + qflx_tile
  - coupler: qflx_rofliq_qsur_grc is the gridcell average of (qflx_surf + qflx_tile) and is sent
    as Flrl_rofsur, so MOSART treats the tile water as surface input. Flrl_rofsub (from
    qflx_drain) does not contain it.
  - BalanceCheck subtracts qflx_tile (it is not in qflx_surf, qflx_h2osfc_surf or qflx_drain).
  - Nitrate: the nitrate carried by the tile water is added to smin_no3_runoff_vr (exported as
    Flrl_no3_runoff), taken only from the layers the tile removed water from, weighted by the
    water removed from each layer. smin_no3_leached_vr is unchanged from release-clm5.0.34.
  - qflx_tile is kept separate from qflx_surf_col on purpose: the existing surface nitrate loss
    uses qflx_surf with a 5 cm mixing depth and would otherwise take the tile nitrate from the
    top 5 cm instead of the drained layers.

The tile drain is done in both subsurface drainage paths, in the same column loop as the
baseflow and after rsub_top has updated h2osoi_liq and zwt:
  - SoilHydrologyMod:Drainage            (TOPMODEL baseflow; lower_boundary_condition = bc_waterTable/bc_aquifer)
  - SoilHydrologyMod:LateralFlowPowerLaw (default CLM5 and use_bedrock; lower_boundary_condition = bc_zero_flux)
Both call one shared routine, TileDrainColumn.

CTSM Master Tag This Corresponds To: N/A (branch clm5-TileDrain of release-clm5.0.34)

Summary of changes:
-------------------

Issues fixed (include CTSM Issue #): None

Science changes since: 9d390bf78
  Linear tile drain, off by default (use_tile_drain = .false.):
     qflx_tile = tile_rate * (tile_depth - zwt)  when zwt is above the drain (mm H2O/s)
  - Water is removed from the saturated layers between the water table and the drain, starting
    at the layer containing the drain and working upward. Each layer gives up no more than
    h2osoi_liq - watmin, and no more than s_y*(saturated thickness above the drain). qflx_tile
    is the water actually removed divided by dtime, so the watmin fixers (which adjust rsub_top
    or qflx_rsub_sat only) never refill a layer the tile emptied and no water is created.
  - zwt is deepened by (water removed)/s_y, with the same analytical specific yield used by
    the TOPMODEL / power-law baseflow blocks, so baseflow does not stay high on top of the
    tile flux. The s_y cap above also keeps zwt from going below the drain. jwt is recomputed.
  - No tile flow if the layer containing the drain is frozen (t_soisno <= tfrz).
  - The drain can be no deeper than the deepest layer water can leave from: nlevsoi in Drainage,
    nbedrock(c) in LateralFlowPowerLaw.
  - Tile drains are only placed on natural vegetation (istsoil) and crop (istcrop) columns.
    Wetland and land ice columns recompute qflx_qrgwl from their own water balance after
    Drainage, which would count the water the tile had already removed a second time.
  - Tile water leaves as surface runoff (see above), and tile nitrate leaves as nitrate runoff
    (use_nitrif_denitrif and use_vertsoilc): smin_no3_runoff_vr gets disn_conc*qflx_tile_vr(c,j)/dz
    in addition to the existing surface-runoff term, before its existing limits. Identical to
    the previous code when use_tile_drain is off.

Software changes since: 9d390bf78
  - SoilHydrologyMod: new private TileDrainColumn (shared by Drainage and LateralFlowPowerLaw);
    both routines zero qflx_tile/qflx_tile_vr in their initial set. qflx_drain is unchanged.
  - LateralFlowPowerLaw gets a new trailing argument, temperature_inst (frozen check); the one
    call in HydrologyDrainageMod is updated.
  - HydrologyDrainageMod: "+ qflx_tile(c)" added to the qflx_runoff sum.
  - lnd2atmMod: qflx_rofliq_qsur_grc now averages qflx_surf_col + qflx_tile_col (new local
    qflx_surf_tile_col; the tile term is only added on active columns).
  - BalanceCheckMod: qflx_tile subtracted in both water-balance sums (default and Fan groundwater
    schemes) and printed in the error diagnostics.
  - WaterfluxType: new qflx_tile_col (col) and qflx_tile_vr_col (col,1:nlevsoi); both zeroed in
