Changes to User Interface since: 9d390bf78
  New namelist items (group clm_inparm):
     use_tile_drain    = .false. (default)  turn tile drainage on
     tile_drain_everywhere = .false. (default)  if .true., ignore TILE_DRAIN on the surface
                                       dataset and drain every soil and crop column (testing
                                       only; leave .false. for production so that a missing
                                       TILE_DRAIN aborts the run)
     tile_drain_depth  = 1.0     (m)        depth of the drain below the surface
     tile_drain_rate   = 5.0e-5  (mm H2O/s per m of water table above the drain)
  tile_drain_depth and tile_drain_rate are placeholder defaults and should be set for the study.
  New surface dataset variable (gridcell): TILE_DRAIN, required only when use_tile_drain = .true.
  and tile_drain_everywhere = .false.
  New history field: QTILE (mm/s). It is separate from QDRAI and QOVER, is a term of total runoff
  (QRUNOFF), and is part of the surface runoff sent to the river model.

Known limits:
